    {
      "id": "ledger-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "Established on the `cas-certificate` route, in the geometry family. Read this fact together with the one it is easiest to confuse it with: `the altitudes are concurrent` in the incidence form proved here is UNCONDITIONAL, whereas `the point where they meet is such-and-such' would not be. The same split is exhibited concretely by F:geometry-medians-concurrent (unconditional) versus F:geometry-centroid-divides-medians (needs a non-degeneracy condition, with a committed counterexample).",
        "type": "prose"
      },
      "provenance": {
